{
  "about": "English palette from vanilla tiles only (stand-ins until the UK tile pack). Wall sets: Tile_creator findings, LOG 2026-10-05. Gable caps per style to match its wall and chimney stacks (fixtures_fireplaces_01, as Riverside's) (LOG 2026-10-07). Shop fronts (with Erika's Tiles): painted timber storefronts in heritage colours - black, bottle green, oxblood, cream, brown - picked per shop by its OSM id like the wall styles; no shop signs (Erika's are American names) (LOG 2026-10-10). The 1960s-70s estate house's style uk_estate_70s is asset_creator/housing_kit's (LOG 2026-10-19 #6/#7). Upper floors, porches and bays per style (upper_wall, porch, bay: export_regional; LOG 2026-10-19 #9). The 1990s superstores' styles uk_superstore_brick / uk_superstore_buff are asset_creator/commercial_kit's (supermarket.py; LOG 2026-10-20 #6): brick to the eaves (user, 2026-10-20: no cladding on the supermarkets), set by export_regional.uk_shopfronts. The industrial units' styles uk_unit_juniper / uk_unit_grey (commercial_kit/industrial.py; LOG 2026-10-20 #9): profiled cladding over a brick dado, a flat roof, a roller shutter (export_regional.uk_units). The farm buildings' styles uk_barn_black_iron / _tile, uk_shed_yorkshire (commercial_kit/farm.py; LOG 2026-10-20 #12): tarred weatherboarding on a brick plinth under corrugated iron or clay tile, Yorkshire boarding over block under fibre cement; no windows, cart or sliding doors (export_regional.uk_farm). granary_staddle (commercial_kit/farm.py; LOG 2026-10-20 #15): a listed granary on staddle stones, the listed maker's wall for a barn whose listing names staddles. uk_garage_brick (commercial_kit; LOG 2026-10-20 #16): a repair garage's workshop in plain red brick, a cream roller shutter, an MOT board (export_regional.uk_garages). uk_exchange_buff (commercial_kit; LOG 2026-10-20 #18): a 1960s telephone exchange, buff brick to a flat roof, a van door, TELEPHONE EXCHANGE in cast letters (export_regional.uk_exchanges).",
